# =====================================================================
# Root .dockerignore — keeps the build context lean so frontend/Dockerfile
# (multi-stage panel SPA + Astro public site, context: repo root) doesn't
# upload 10+ GB of voct_data, node_modules, and .git over the wire.
# =====================================================================

# VCS
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Environment files — secrets stay on the host; the Dockerfile receives
# every VITE_* / PUBLIC_* explicitly via build ARGs in docker-compose.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
backend/.env
frontend/.env
frontend/.env.local
web/.env
web/.env.production

# ---- Node / npm artefacts (will be installed fresh inside the image) ----
**/node_modules
**/npm-debug.log
**/yarn-error.log
**/pnpm-debug.log

# ---- Frontend build / cache ----
frontend/dist
frontend/.vite
frontend/coverage

# ---- Web (Astro) build / cache ----
# Astro's dist/ is regenerated inside the image by the web-builder stage.
# .astro is its generated content-collection types cache; also regenerated.
web/dist
web/.astro

# The full-size camera archive, and a retired backdrop set kept for reference. Neither is read
# by the build: Astro globs `src/assets/photos/*` FLAT (lib/photos.ts), and the proxies it does
# glob are generated from the archive by `npm run photos:proxy` on the host, before the image is
# built. Letting these into the context would put ~530 MB straight back into the `COPY web/ ./`
# layer — the weight the proxies exist to remove, and what pushes BuildKit past the GC_KEEP
# budget in infra/docker-gc.sh and evicts the Astro image cache the next build needs.
web/src/assets/photos/.original-photos
web/src/assets/photos/.old-bg-desktop

# Grading samples for the church interior — ~98 MB of frames kept beside the proxies so the
# choice can be re-made against the originals. The photo glob is FLAT (`*`), so no build reads
# them; without this line they ride into the `COPY web/ ./` layer anyway, for the same reason
# and at the same cost as the archive above.
web/src/assets/photos/kosciol-samples

# Video, in both its homes, and for one reason: no build step reads a frame of it.
#  • `src/assets/videos/` holds the camera masters and the encodes made from them — a host-side
#    step, the same shape as `npm run photos:proxy` above.
#  • `public/video/` holds the six files the site actually serves. They reach nginx through the
#    bind mount in docker-compose.prod.yml, NOT through an image layer, which is the whole point:
#    everything under public/ is otherwise copied verbatim into dist/ and baked in.
# Together they are ~1.7 GB that used to ride the `COPY web/ ./` layer, get hashed by rollup,
# land in dist/, and be copied into the image a second time — 29 minutes of asset pass per
# deploy, and the BuildKit budget blown by records nothing would reuse.
#
# CONSEQUENCE, and it is the failure worth recognising: with the mount missing on a host, the
# films 404 and everything else on the page is fine. Check the volume before suspecting the code.
web/src/assets/videos
web/public/video

# ---- Python / Django (the backend has its OWN Dockerfile + context: ./backend,
# but anything that would slip into this root context should still be excluded
# in case the root image ever needs to reach in.) ----
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
backend/venv
backend/env
backend/.pytest_cache
backend/htmlcov
backend/.mypy_cache
backend/.ruff_cache
backend/db.sqlite3
**/*.sqlite3
backend/media
backend/static
backend/staticfiles

# ---- Host-side runtime data (Compose bind-mounts) — never enters the image ----
voct_data/

# ---- Tooling caches ----
.parcel-cache
.cache
.turbo
.next
.output

# ---- Documentation that doesn't belong in the runtime image ----
docs/
*.md
!frontend/README.md
!web/README.md
# (the two READMEs above are kept only because some tooling reads metadata
# from them — strip them if image size matters more than introspection.)

# Local A/B video clips (web/.gitignore too). Everything under public/ is copied verbatim into
# dist/ by the web-builder stage, so without this the grading samples would ship to nginx.
web/public/probki
